# Architecture & Framework Rules

- Use Astro (latest version) with its content collections, View Transitions API, and hybrid rendering capabilities.
- Favor static generation (SSG) for all pages whenever possible.
- Only hydrate React islands when absolutely necessary (e.g., for the window manager or other interactive UI).
- Prefer Astro components for static content and layout.
- Implement progressive enhancement — everything should work without JavaScript enabled (except movable windows).
- Maintain zero or minimal client-side JS footprint unless interactivity is required.
